#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157697 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5fb547a-2518-5db9-b1b1-aab8d80328af" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using VOP When the Forcing Term is Part of the Complementary Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d8ac9a8-e6c6-5d34-9330-72ee02f31f3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x)e^{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155410} {:answer/id #uuid "f57a3f79-89e7-53e0-a992-b2d38bdcaa1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x)e^{− 2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155411} {:answer/id #uuid "1b574d2d-2d4f-5bee-a562-61f6efa27b28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x)e^{− 4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155412} {:answer/id #uuid "4343e134-7b50-5ba1-b628-f7d98d4a10f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x)e^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155413} {:answer/id #uuid "673adad6-2ed2-5d8d-8618-810b4994ec68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x)e^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "673adad6-2ed2-5d8d-8618-810b4994ec68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x)e^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155414} :answer-field/id #uuid "720115ae-6071-5d81-a2ab-1fdfcc5efcc5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155409} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a67ae763-8737-5ca8-8563-98aa05e2ef72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xe^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155416} {:answer/id #uuid "aa9cd4dc-a8a5-5e66-b2ba-df613f28902f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xe^{− 4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155417} {:answer/id #uuid "e77e1ae6-19db-52cc-8781-7ac8711e0808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{− 4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155418} {:answer/id #uuid "440ae774-230a-5fe6-a975-502ae84424e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a67ae763-8737-5ca8-8563-98aa05e2ef72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xe^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155416} :answer-field/id #uuid "c68a2547-8586-5b7d-84c6-0b0d23fbb6b7" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155415} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab711ee9-d698-5c04-86f2-3c008766ee74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155421} {:answer/id #uuid "b1ace21b-528a-50d6-8233-6bf8a67818af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xe^{− 4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155422} {:answer/id #uuid "cb37b776-f2f9-5ea7-80ec-ed640437cf9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155423} {:answer/id #uuid "df88e8c3-53b8-5ed4-8aa2-7ac0aa5bde73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155424} {:answer/id #uuid "40faae26-10c4-5c8d-a430-856c86a6ba4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xe^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155425} {:answer/id #uuid "45bebca2-3c99-5418-b281-f7b5970ff98d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{− 4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab711ee9-d698-5c04-86f2-3c008766ee74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155421} :answer-field/id #uuid "fddcab0c-b9eb-5c69-b36a-133f454ea22e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155420}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "171f0292-ff02-54bb-a27d-4ba2f7ec9f11" :question/math-academy-id "q-337177" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4y={e}^{4x}.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below. \n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-4{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{4x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{4x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{4x})}^{′}-4(u{e}^{4x}) & ={e}^{4x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{4x}+4u{e}^{4x}-4u{e}^{4x} & ={e}^{4x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{4x}+\\cancel{4u{e}^{4x}}-\\cancel{4u{e}^{4x}} & ={e}^{4x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{4x} & ={e}^{4x} \\\\ {u}^{′} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =1 \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{4x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{4x} \\\\  & =x{e}^{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363076 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ac34a18-053d-5eab-8c2c-bd0f15658186" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9c5dcb2-cebd-565b-a414-f1f6198f9f45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363078} {:answer/id #uuid "bf91ad93-f4fc-57c1-b550-94972f6af7f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363079} {:answer/id #uuid "7ac95a8a-ee51-585b-9a6e-f0b5bc80ae5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363080} {:answer/id #uuid "9a37f52f-19f5-5348-8b18-bbb6d57b341b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363081} {:answer/id #uuid "11676e06-4095-5f0d-92c7-faa115376ebb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf91ad93-f4fc-57c1-b550-94972f6af7f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363079} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb87f899-5dbf-5dd3-a094-edb96e87079c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363077} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7637701c-fa72-509f-aa13-3dec62fbdb73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363084} {:answer/id #uuid "22ae1a5e-df34-5acc-a5cb-84b053344274" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363085} {:answer/id #uuid "a19e3d0d-240b-5a96-8592-db2cc03b0a0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363086} {:answer/id #uuid "76f76ec5-11db-5138-986e-714eaed46f32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363087} {:answer/id #uuid "2f91e518-2425-58c2-8d15-75fcd373b238" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a19e3d0d-240b-5a96-8592-db2cc03b0a0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363086} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dfaee88-2c62-5f61-9548-cd01556e6bc9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363083} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3e2670b-0197-5c08-ad7f-dd7370195002" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363090} {:answer/id #uuid "f7ee10cd-fa47-5b46-ba62-d2f960e5ed4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363091} {:answer/id #uuid "fcdfef37-bbf8-5505-9a2a-cfffb5967343" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363092} {:answer/id #uuid "a9635bcb-87ba-5bd9-821a-7bc306af97dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363093} {:answer/id #uuid "da24722d-c932-5e0a-aa9b-4a0d98d8c45c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363094}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3e2670b-0197-5c08-ad7f-dd7370195002" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363090} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cf65468-a280-5820-8d43-208415e4d045" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a01f9794-773d-5e12-a888-6dc684788a68" :question/math-academy-id "q-337376" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=5.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-3{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{3x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{3x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{3x})}^{′}-3(u{e}^{3x}) & =5 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x}+3u{e}^{3x}-3u{e}^{3x} & =5 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x}+\\cancel{3u{e}^{3x}}-\\cancel{3u{e}^{3x}} & =5 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x} & =5 \\\\ {u}^{′} & =5{e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =5{e}^{-3x} \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 5{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{-3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{3x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{3x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{-3x}\\cdot {e}^{3x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363095 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ac34a18-053d-5eab-8c2c-bd0f15658186" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1ac3957-5174-57d1-a973-90edce9bd8ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363097} {:answer/id #uuid "9eafaf0e-0d87-521f-9946-b9d3730e99a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363098} {:answer/id #uuid "b41e2c24-5887-569b-ac33-8c5e7e9bbfe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363099} {:answer/id #uuid "202aaccc-96ae-52e4-9820-fef38221c8df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363100} {:answer/id #uuid "fdba04b0-8008-559f-951c-526e8f5121b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9eafaf0e-0d87-521f-9946-b9d3730e99a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363098} :answer-field/id #uuid "bea36b64-3c06-5d88-aec7-3fc1a9f51d5f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363096} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c345317-51eb-56dd-9c09-e03d2d991e2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363103} {:answer/id #uuid "d961779a-e938-5518-8c3b-f6a507f15ce2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363104} {:answer/id #uuid "458d4688-d5c4-5050-9033-141073d9e4a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363105} {:answer/id #uuid "99856b47-3555-5bc0-ae0e-1ee90c0926bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "458d4688-d5c4-5050-9033-141073d9e4a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363105} :answer-field/id #uuid "0379f37f-6797-5716-be84-9d7ee71e8340" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363102} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43df3ede-9170-5b62-aab8-132f85d8798c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363108} {:answer/id #uuid "8993529e-70ed-586b-b58f-5783de9b04ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}\\int {e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363109} {:answer/id #uuid "5dd92b8f-e4a2-5087-a5ab-e74f7c2f5211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363110} {:answer/id #uuid "3e46f135-3346-5e39-b1e3-38e1e1f527f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dd92b8f-e4a2-5087-a5ab-e74f7c2f5211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363110} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac29e0bc-e5b6-5a99-ba75-068f46f3dafe" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363107}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a129942b-bc96-5e41-9abc-674cc7d1e75b" :question/math-academy-id "q-337399" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+2{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-2x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-2x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{-2x})}^{′}+2(u{e}^{-2x}) & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-2x}-2u{e}^{-2x}+2u{e}^{-2x} & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-2x}-\\cancel{2u{e}^{-2x}}+\\cancel{2u{e}^{-2x}} & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-2x} & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′} & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{-2x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{-2x} \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {e}^{-2x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5fb547a-2518-5db9-b1b1-aab8d80328af" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using VOP When the Forcing Term is Part of the Complementary Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdcb4b5b-884d-58a8-addc-7ce0e64ad91b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363114} {:answer/id #uuid "79d6cf47-ac82-56c0-ab62-0d27a1561aea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363115} {:answer/id #uuid "9f464da3-f1d6-5840-85fd-765d09a8acb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363116} {:answer/id #uuid "7f33d57a-9952-5af7-8cfe-d01e8664b1a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{15x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363117} {:answer/id #uuid "eb8281e8-aa00-54b3-8522-43f12a25a0c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f464da3-f1d6-5840-85fd-765d09a8acb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363116} :answer-field/id #uuid "f30a8b5c-cda7-5b6a-ac19-afc6dcbfa075" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363113} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0357fc3a-37b2-54b8-ab60-f3da5ca5f828" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363120} {:answer/id #uuid "96ed7b5b-2943-51e3-9315-ef9a6bcf696e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363121} {:answer/id #uuid "b921c5fc-87f2-5c81-a9da-0a9103cb8997" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363122} {:answer/id #uuid "4191bd90-ffb7-5e23-976d-46e6e65821d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-x{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b921c5fc-87f2-5c81-a9da-0a9103cb8997" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363122} :answer-field/id #uuid "18e52400-1add-599a-9ab6-7a950dabc40b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363119} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bace0ea-9395-52aa-9d5f-8ba764b46e60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x{e}^{5x}-{e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363125} {:answer/id #uuid "3a21437a-d2bf-5240-ae9c-328d5ccf766f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5x}-x{e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363126} {:answer/id #uuid "756efd21-00ed-5ce4-834f-6a21fc5bb3ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5x}-\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363127} {:answer/id #uuid "e010c3b9-5c77-5f4b-8478-c5bfa85acd93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x{e}^{5x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e010c3b9-5c77-5f4b-8478-c5bfa85acd93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x{e}^{5x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363128} :answer-field/id #uuid "85a9e798-3199-546c-b623-aefe1dcddb6f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363124}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5bf23900-2f3d-53c0-9448-69b2b01a2a2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-337488" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y=10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-5{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{5x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{5x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{5x})}^{′}-5(u{e}^{5x}) & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{5x}+5u{e}^{5x}-5u{e}^{5x} & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{5x}+\\cancel{5u{e}^{5x}}-\\cancel{5u{e}^{5x}} & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{5x} & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′} & =10{e}^{-5x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x=\\frac{{e}^{5x}+{e}^{-5x}}{2}\n$$\n\nour equation for $u$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =10{e}^{-5x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\  & =10{e}^{-5x}(\\frac{{e}^{5x}+{e}^{-5x}}{2}) \\\\  & =5{e}^{-5x}({e}^{5x}+{e}^{-5x}) \\\\  & =5+5{e}^{-10x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =5+5{e}^{-10x} \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 5+5{e}^{-10x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =5x-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-10x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{5x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{5x} \\\\  & =5x{e}^{5x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-5x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363129 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5fb547a-2518-5db9-b1b1-aab8d80328af" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using VOP When the Forcing Term is Part of the Complementary Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03e16c96-e6e3-5d67-88a1-f1f496e8d91f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363131} {:answer/id #uuid "ad26962a-0a31-5443-9d04-672f1a357fea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363132} {:answer/id #uuid "ce2e93da-ee4e-5a57-890c-baa42ae0c28b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363133} {:answer/id #uuid "be5d56fa-72ed-5b41-8f79-78e6a2e48fe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{15x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363134} {:answer/id #uuid "902a7f87-d433-518a-823c-855c2867691c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce2e93da-ee4e-5a57-890c-baa42ae0c28b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363133} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5dad03a-7662-58cb-8320-653014df7b50" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363130} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31bac67c-2104-5e27-a89c-e9d447b2481e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+x{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363137} {:answer/id #uuid "2b63ff82-80de-54eb-9f0b-857ea6cecac1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x+{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363138} {:answer/id #uuid "1849aaff-88da-5987-a140-c1459c247844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x+2{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363139} {:answer/id #uuid "1457605b-2781-5b7c-ac88-7362c9318175" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+2x{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b63ff82-80de-54eb-9f0b-857ea6cecac1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x+{e}^{-10x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363138} :answer-field/id #uuid "7339de18-2e64-5e3d-ad3e-f214452af80d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363136} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "feef1e7a-979a-5f7a-90e9-0d9a287ce5fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5x}+2x{e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363142} {:answer/id #uuid "6f858996-a983-5805-9f56-9294928f17e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x{e}^{5x}+{e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363143} {:answer/id #uuid "61ab140c-f0b0-5a41-b9b4-c448e4bbb805" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5x}+x{e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363144} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e244eb-89e1-5c7f-b546-41694411386a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x{e}^{5x}+2{e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f858996-a983-5805-9f56-9294928f17e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x{e}^{5x}+{e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363143} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a637610-9f3e-5843-ae2c-b744dd3e59d7" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363141}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54ef0c16-1df4-5060-9377-447e0ea12bfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-337524" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y=20\\operatorname{sinh}⁡5x.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-5{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{5x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{5x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{5x})}^{′}-5(u{e}^{5x}) & =20\\operatorname{sinh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{5x}+5u{e}^{5x}-5u{e}^{5x} & =20\\operatorname{sinh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{5x}+\\cancel{5u{e}^{5x}}-\\cancel{5u{e}^{5x}} & =20\\operatorname{sinh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{5x} & =20\\operatorname{sinh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′} & =20{e}^{-5x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡5x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}⁡5x=\\frac{{e}^{5x}-{e}^{-5x}}{2}\n$$\n\nour equation for $u$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =20{e}^{-5x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡5x \\\\  & =20{e}^{-5x}(\\frac{{e}^{5x}-{e}^{-5x}}{2}) \\\\  & =10{e}^{-5x}({e}^{5x}-{e}^{-5x}) \\\\  & =10-10{e}^{-10x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =10-10{e}^{-10x} \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 10-10{e}^{-10x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =10x+{e}^{-10x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{5x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{5x} \\\\  & =10x{e}^{5x}+{e}^{-5x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
